# fixedbugs, defect 588, lane b19-dep, 2026-10-10 (panel 208's R2).
#
# SYMPTOM: a function its header marks `__attribute__((unavailable))`, bound
# and never called, exited 2 with *internal error: compiling the generated C
# failed* and clang's text at the compiler's own probe of the binding: the
# header's refusal blamed on the compiler.
#
# FIX: `emit/ffi_unavailable.hero` reads clang's `'gone' is unavailable` wherever
# the unit names the binding, and where a group of this program declares the
# name it is told `ffi_unavailable` on the binding, at exit 1, the header's
# own words in a note (panel 208's R2; `.claude/rules/c-boundary.md`).

extern "fixedbugs-588-unavailable.h"
    function gone(x: i64) -> i64  #~ ffi_unavailable
    function kept(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(kept(x: 6))
